WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:05.743
- We must, we must
start pushing on intent.

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:11.025
We should fix our intent, not
our ability to check the box.

00:00:11.025 --> 00:00:13.250
(upbeat music)

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:15.069
- You got your perspective.

00:00:15.069 --> 00:00:18.378
(crowd cheers)

00:00:18.378 --> 00:00:20.473
I just wanna be happy,
don't you wanna be happy?

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:25.580
I'm about to talk to you about why

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:27.940
I believe kindness and empathy

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:32.180
and every other great
emotional intelligence skill

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:33.970
is the foundation to actually build

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:37.380
a great business, financially, money.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:41.334
And yet, I'm the child of a father

00:00:41.334 --> 00:00:43.870
who grew up in the Soviet Union.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:47.110
I was born there as well,
came here when I was three.

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:51.210
And when my dad eventually
achieved his American dream

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:53.980
and owned a liquor
store, when I was dragged

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:55.910
into that liquor store as a 14-year old,

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:57.520
my dad sat me down,

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:01.240
and this is the singular
first piece of advice

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:04.030
that I heard in the real business world.

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:04.980
'Cause I was crushing it

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:06.944
in lemonade stands and baseball cards.

00:01:06.944 --> 00:01:08.020
(audience laughs)

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:10.230
But this was the first
thing I had ever heard.

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:13.040
My dad and I are driving
to the liquor store.

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:16.890
My dad is really in a lot
of ways the reverse of me,

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:18.923
which means he doesn't talk a whole lot.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:23.820
But he looked at me, and before
we walked into the store,

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:26.270
he looked me dead in the face.

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:28.450
And my dad's one of these
guys with like eyebrows

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:30.515
that are naturally in the mean position.

00:01:30.515 --> 00:01:31.850
(audience laughs)

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:34.230
Doesn't speak, and is
from the Soviet Union,

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:35.490
and looks me dead in the face

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:39.837
and says to me, "The
employees are our enemies."

00:01:39.837 --> 00:01:42.670
(audience laughs)

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.627
He said, "Son, the only thing you have

00:01:46.627 --> 00:01:50.367
"to do today in the store, is
to make sure you watch them,

00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:51.952
"so they don't steal."

00:01:51.952 --> 00:01:54.100
(audience laughs)

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:58.680
And I used to really hate,
be mad at and worst of all,

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:01.440
judge my father for that.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:05.770
And I did that because I
lacked empathy and context

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:08.640
and understanding that when
you're first 22 years or

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:12.700
in the Soviet union and
communism owns everything,

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:15.270
the entire world works
with the black market

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:16.470
and everybody steals.

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:18.510
And that's just how the ecosystem works.

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:22.990
But it's so full circle for me
to have the incredible luxury

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:25.640
of being here tonight and an honor

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:30.640
because my natural DNA was
far more like my mother's.

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:34.170
I genuinely believe
that karma is practical.

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:38.870
I wildly believe in optimism
to the point of delusion.

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:42.540
My greatest weaknesses
over the last 20 years

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:45.660
in running businesses has
actually been predicated

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:47.940
in creating entitlement.

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:51.640
Because I care so much
about EQ and optimism

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:56.270
and we can figure it out to
the point where no question

00:02:56.270 --> 00:02:59.770
my great regret as a CEO
for the last 20 years

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:01.360
in two different
businesses with the success

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:03.640
that I've had is that
there are people walking

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:06.520
around the world that I
did the wrong thing by

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:10.470
because I love happiness
so much that I was unable

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:14.440
to have the gear of radical
candor that is needed

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:17.200
to offset everything
I'm about to talk about.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:21.400
However, to this day I would
much rather have a culture

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:26.170
of happy, and safe, and entitled.

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:30.190
Then wildly profitable and dark.

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:32.800
And I believe we're sitting
in a very interesting time.

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:35.810
A time we're in culture in the macro,

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:37.700
we are pulling in opposite directions,

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:41.520
thinking somehow miraculously
one way of doing things

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:45.440
is the right way and yet
to achieve everything

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:50.440
I'm about to talk about,
which is 100% accountability.

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:53.230
Recognizing that us judging employees when

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:57.140
we navigate companies
based on a P&amp;L is ludicrous

00:03:57.140 --> 00:04:00.780
and audacious and unkind in a world where

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:03.880
I genuinely believe
that, you know, actually,

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:06.300
let me throw this in here and
this may help frame it up.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:08.320
When I think about being a
media, my current company,

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:11.440
900 people, global, Singapore,
London, New York, LA,

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:12.480
it's an agency.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:13.313
Tough game.

00:04:13.313 --> 00:04:14.770
Client services is brutal.

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:16.640
It's a real rugged game.

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:19.490
I believe that I've done
a lot of things wrong

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:22.370
and a lot of things right,
but I believe genuinely

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:25.300
that the reason the organization
continues to flourish

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:29.150
is because we look at
it as the honey empire.

00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:31.240
Honey over vinegar.

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:34.440
There is no reason not to
be kind and compassionate.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.810
The meta nature of what
transpired today in

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:39.770
my organization without
going into him or her today,

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:43.560
literally today, my organization fired one

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:46.120
of the single most productive
financial employees

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:49.440
in our company for 100% reason of

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:54.180
he is just not a good communicator
or she too, Goddammit.

00:04:56.267 --> 00:04:59.100
(audience laughs)

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:03.150
There's just not a good
communicator to people around them.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:04.890
I do not know how to say this

00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:06.600
in any other words than the following;

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:08.580
I believe the technology advancements

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:11.910
over the next half century
will prove out the hypothesis

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:15.320
that I will lay in front of
you, which is the following;

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:19.220
making decisions far more
predicated around people

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:21.780
that have humility.

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:24.080
People that have kindness,

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:28.610
generally likable people drives
bigger financial results,

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:29.443
period.

00:05:29.443 --> 00:05:33.850
End of story and let us
collectively look ourselves

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:36.440
in the mirror and understand
that the far majority

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:37.690
of businesses that are

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:42.690
in corporate land are
run by CFOs, not CEOs.

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:49.040
And let us accept that
a CFO that she or he has

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:52.550
to navigate an organization to make

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:55.920
its payroll to hit its numbers.

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:58.150
I think we judge, there
are many people here

00:05:58.150 --> 00:05:59.520
in the HR profession.

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:03.260
You know I for a long time
called myself an HR driven CEO.

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:05.760
You can watch videos of me
in 2007 on the internet.

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:10.760
Fat me talking about that
long before this was cool,

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:13.640
long before this was in the consciousness.

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:15.560
But it took me an evolution
to understand the thing

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:17.320
I opened with because I
wanted to get right to it,

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:20.240
which is I wasn't finding
the right balance.

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:22.180
It was a little bit too much optimism.

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:25.260
I had to find the cadence
and now I navigate

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:28.050
and more importantly because
I hate focus groups of one,

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:32.250
I watch and analyze and
look at so many businesses.

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:34.170
I believe that you can have both.

00:06:34.170 --> 00:06:36.350
I believe that you can have both.

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:40.380
I believe that there is an
unbelievably powerful opportunity

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:43.699
for businesses to have
friction between the CFO

00:06:43.699 --> 00:06:46.810
and as we call it at VaynerMedia,
the chief heart officer.

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:50.190
Claude silver holds this
position in my organization.

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:52.020
She is my direct report.

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:52.853
Not only that,

00:06:52.853 --> 00:06:55.580
she is the number two person
within our organization.

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:59.853
Weekly, monthly, we sit
and have strategy, people,

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:04.890
business meetings where if her

00:07:04.890 --> 00:07:06.780
and the CFO do not see eye to eye,

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:09.440
the tie goes to the rudder to her.

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:13.480
That is wildly unheard
of in our society today

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:15.810
and much like most of the things

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:19.910
that I've had my hand in historically,

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:21.500
it becomes correct.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:26.500
Is there so much naivete at the
wall street, Silicon Valley,

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:30.980
business alpha DNA to not
understand that retention

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:35.420
and happiness leads to
dramatic more results

00:07:35.420 --> 00:07:39.200
than appeasing the best
salesperson even though

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:41.040
they have a tornado and wipe out

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:44.037
everybody internally in their path.

00:07:44.037 --> 00:07:45.700
(audience applauds)

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:47.900
I appreciate that sir, 'cause it's right.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:49.650
In actually--
(audience applauds)

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:52.530
I have come to realize
something remarkable.

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:54.930
Growing up in a family
liquor store business where

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:56.350
your business paid for your life.

00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:59.640
So this was not about awards
or weird reports or theory.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:03.230
This was life and then
going into startup world

00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:05.490
where I invested, it was life to come

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:08.320
into corporate land over the last decade.

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:12.190
I am fascinated by the
ability of corporate America

00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:14.070
and global corporate organizations

00:08:14.070 --> 00:08:17.970
to have somehow systematically
eliminated common sense

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:19.142
from the equation.

00:08:19.142 --> 00:08:21.642
(phone rings)

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:25.010
Hey guys, sorry to interrupt your video.

00:08:25.010 --> 00:08:27.900
I'm just giving you this
call for my number to let

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:30.709
you know that you have to
join my text community.

00:08:30.709 --> 00:08:33.480
(212) 931-5731.

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:34.710
Hit me up with a text.

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:39.710
If common sense had a place
in current big business,

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:42.190
we wouldn't even need to talk about HR.

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:45.200
It's people.

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:47.040
It's always gonna be people.

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:49.310
Nobody's paying more
attention to blockchain

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:51.750
and AI and machine learning
and all that than me

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:55.020
and I promise you, it's going to be people

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:58.671
until the robots come
along and kill all of us.

00:08:58.671 --> 00:08:59.880
(audience laughs)

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:01.130
which I think they might.

00:09:02.970 --> 00:09:04.600
It's going to be people.

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:09.600
We have to start getting much
smarter around hidden costs.

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:12.800
Letting go of somebody to hit a number

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:15.470
who's kinda something on the numbers,

00:09:15.470 --> 00:09:19.280
but is the beat, the heart, the glue and

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:21.880
it makes 12 other people want
to come to an organization.

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:25.489
That person needs to be
rewarded financially, not fired.

00:09:25.489 --> 00:09:28.489
(audience applauds)

00:09:31.257 --> 00:09:33.908
And before this gets way too foofy foofy!

00:09:33.908 --> 00:09:35.220
(audience laughs)

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:36.440
I wanna remind everybody that

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:39.593
I think of my organization
as the honey empire.

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:42.900
I am out here to put
everybody out of business.

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:43.980
I wanna win.

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:46.190
I wanna build the biggest
company in the world.

00:09:46.190 --> 00:09:48.373
I wanna buy the New York jets

00:09:48.373 --> 00:09:50.432
and win a Superbowl and then die.

00:09:50.432 --> 00:09:53.265
(audience laughs)

00:09:54.730 --> 00:09:57.370
Not knowing anything about the real world

00:09:57.370 --> 00:09:58.930
because I was a terrible student and

00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:00.690
I was completely 100% focused

00:10:00.690 --> 00:10:02.960
on the end consumer
always lemonade stands,

00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:05.923
baseball cards, the wine
business, VaynerMedia.

00:10:07.430 --> 00:10:10.060
I didn't even know these
conversations existed.

00:10:10.060 --> 00:10:12.300
I don't even understand
what we're debating.

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:16.340
How can you have an organization
when the asset is people

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:18.660
where that is not the thing we
spend the most time and then

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:20.800
I understood, Oh, weird, right?

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:22.730
Because I was a DNF student.

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:26.373
I'm not good at black and
white, but I dominate gray.

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:29.720
I dominate gray, right?

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:32.620
People don't have the
emotional intuitive luck

00:10:32.620 --> 00:10:33.453
of the draw.

00:10:33.453 --> 00:10:34.286
Some of you, I'm looking around.

00:10:34.286 --> 00:10:37.050
Some of you are just born really pretty.

00:10:37.050 --> 00:10:40.440
Some of you are fast,
some of you are tall.

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:43.890
Some people just get it
when it comes to people

00:10:43.890 --> 00:10:46.810
and if you get it when it comes to people,

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:48.030
you have to start leaning

00:10:48.030 --> 00:10:51.990
into things like empathy, compassion.

00:10:51.990 --> 00:10:53.930
You have to become much more thoughtful.

00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:56.030
All our political stuff right now,

00:10:56.030 --> 00:10:58.940
nobody's deploying any empathy to anybody.

00:10:58.940 --> 00:11:00.720
Everybody's on tilt.

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:03.300
Everybody's on their point of view.

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:05.090
That's happening in our society.

00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:07.220
It's happening definitely
within the four walls

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:10.560
of our organizations and at the tippy top.

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:14.120
This is just one bad game of wall street

00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:16.700
and I'm not mad at wall
street even though....

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:17.805
I'm not mad.

00:11:17.805 --> 00:11:19.430
(audience laughs)

00:11:19.430 --> 00:11:21.810
I'm mad at games that have to be played

00:11:21.810 --> 00:11:24.580
in every 90 day terms and
if you don't play within

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:27.730
that 90 days, you become vulnerable.

00:11:27.730 --> 00:11:31.810
It's very easy to be the head
of people and make decisions

00:11:31.810 --> 00:11:34.750
around people and be mad at
the CEO and be bad at her,

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:37.900
but you're not the one on
a phone call with investors

00:11:37.900 --> 00:11:40.845
with on wall street every
90 days explaining why.

00:11:40.845 --> 00:11:43.680
Don't worry everybody who's
put their money into us.

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:45.820
A lot of it, good news.

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:48.240
I know that our money looks real bad,

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:50.464
but everyone's super happy.

00:11:50.464 --> 00:11:53.297
(audience laughs)

00:11:54.180 --> 00:11:57.220
Most CEOs don't have the
luxury of having enough control

00:11:57.220 --> 00:12:00.770
to let that play out and really
manifest within a decade.

00:12:00.770 --> 00:12:02.810
Most don't even care.

00:12:02.810 --> 00:12:04.210
Let me promise you one thing.

00:12:04.210 --> 00:12:07.370
If you have some North star of Nirvana,

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:12.370
of businesses that really care
about people and your company

00:12:12.610 --> 00:12:15.170
in one way or another,
ladders up to something

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:16.660
that is publicly traded,

00:12:16.660 --> 00:12:19.883
please stand up and leave Dallas, now.

00:12:21.020 --> 00:12:24.456
I mean that do not be naive and it's,

00:12:24.456 --> 00:12:28.890
there's nothing necessarily
massively wrong with that,

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:30.970
but delusional ideology of the game

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:33.743
you're actually playing
always leads to frustration.

00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:36.640
It's just the way it is.

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:40.990
You wanna be 100% centric
around the people narrative.

00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:43.860
Go become a weird Yoda in a cave and Peru

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:47.290
because if you're in a
business that has a P&amp;L

00:12:47.290 --> 00:12:48.680
that has to hit numbers,

00:12:48.680 --> 00:12:50.920
the other part's gonna
be part of the equation.

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:55.490
But I argue that it has
gone ridiculously too far,

00:12:55.490 --> 00:12:58.340
that in the consolidation
of corporate stuff

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:02.540
and good students that like
numbers and Excel sheets,

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:05.820
we have lost so much of what SMBs

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:09.093
and family businesses have
run on, which is the nuances.

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:13.310
I, out of sheer luck
that my parents had sex

00:13:13.310 --> 00:13:16.610
at the right moment, have the DNA that

00:13:16.610 --> 00:13:18.790
I pulled very hard from both sides.

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:21.210
I pull very hard from both sides.

00:13:21.210 --> 00:13:24.830
I will always choose longterm
people because when I look

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:28.440
at my retention of my employees,

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:31.510
I realize the speed in
which thing navigate

00:13:31.510 --> 00:13:35.480
through knowing each
other and most importantly

00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:39.810
when you have an organization
